# {{lb|en|basketball}} The achievement of a two-digit number of any three of [[point]]s scored, [[assist]]s, [[rebound]]s, [[block]]s, or [[steal]]s in a single [[game]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2016-11-28|author=Mike Vorkunov|title=Despite Flash of Rose’s Prime, Knicks Are Dazed by Westbrook and Thunder|journal=w:The New York Times|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/28/sports/basketball/new-york-knicks-oklahoma-city-thunder.html|passage=Yes, the Knicks had fallen prey to the habitual wizardry of the Thunder star Russell Westbrook, who had 27 points, 18 rebounds and 14 assists, his third straight '''triple-double''' and his eighth in 19 games this season.}}

